---
/**
 * Typographic wrapper for rendered markdown.
 *
 * Tailwind's preflight strips `list-style` and `padding` from lists, and
 * `@tailwindcss/typography` is what puts them back. Markdown rendered outside
 * this wrapper therefore has no bullets, no indent and no paragraph spacing —
 * which is why blog posts read as run-together text rather than a document.
 */
---

<div
  class="prose dark:prose-invert prose-a:text-link-on-light dark:prose-a:text-link prose-p:text-start prose-ul:list-disc text-left">
  <!--
    text-left overrides `body { text-align: justify }` from @layer base.
    Justification with `hyphens: manual` can only pad word-spaces, so long
    words open rivers of whitespace down the column. Prose is the one place
    that matters; the rest of the site keeps its justified layout.

    Deliberately absent: `prose-headings:underline`. @layer base already
    underlines h2 and h3, so setting it here drew a second line.
    Also absent: `prose-a:text-violet-500`. Links take the themed token like
    every other link on the site, rather than a literal that exists in
    neither palette.
  -->
  <slot />
</div>
